Known non-deterministic flake (same one already skipped for z3-4.14.1 and
z3-4.16.0): z3-5.1.0's response to an unsupported get-info/set-info key is
sometimes a clean "unsupported", sometimes a garbled raw help-text dump
("; Suppported get-info parameters: ...") that jSMTLIB can't parse -- the
exact shape differs between runs. A .bad golden (exact-match) can never
stay in sync with genuinely non-deterministic output.

Originally filed as three separate platform-suffixed skips (.linux,
.macos-arm64, .windows), each hedging that it hadn't yet been seen on the
remaining platform(s) -- consolidated into this one bare, platform-independent
skip now that it has also been observed on macos-15-x86_64 (Intel), the one
combination those hedges were still waiting on. Not actually specific to any
platform or architecture; just not deterministic enough to reproduce on
every single run everywhere.

Very likely the same SolverProcess stdout-race root cause as ok_getInfo3.tst.skip.z3-4.14.1 (a stray '; Suppported get-info parameters: ...' diagnostic block leaking across command boundaries under concurrent load) -- see https://github.com/smtlib/jSMTLIB/issues/99.
